WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:06.240
Birds of Prey is being described as a "girl
gang" movie set in the DC cinematic universe,

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:10.730
following Margot Robbie's Harley Quinn as
she takes Gotham City on her own terms.

00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:15.110
Now that we've seen the film's first trailer,
we know more than ever about why these birds

00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:16.380
are flocking together.

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:21.000
As a character, Harley Quinn has largely been
defined by her toxic relationship with the

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:21.760
Joker.

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:26.860
That was certainly the case in 2016's Suicide
Squad, but she's leaving her Puddin' behind

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:28.740
in Cathy Yan's new movie.

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:33.080
The "Fantabulous Emancipation" part of the
title refers to the fact that Harley Quinn

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:36.680
has broken up with the Joker, and she confirms
as much in the trailer.

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:41.410
We see Robbie's character chopping off the
pink and blue-tinged tips of her hair in one

00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:45.260
shot, and this isn't just a play on the fact
that people often enjoy a makeover after a

00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:46.040
breakup.

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:50.560
Harley Quinn's hair was a big part of her
costume in Suicide Squad, and having Robbie

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:55.600
cut it off is seemingly symbolic of the character
moving on from that much-derided movie.

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:58.620
But can she move on from the Joker completely?

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:03.059
The opening shot of the trailer sees Harley
Quinn and her new sidekick Cassandra Cain

00:01:03.059 --> 00:01:07.790
walking down a deserted road with the bright
lights of Gotham's cityscape in the background,

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:12.370
but the purple light in the foreground seems
to suggest that her experiences in the Joker's

00:01:12.370 --> 00:01:15.900
colorful, club-lit world are still following
her for the time being.

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:21.180
One of the standout moments from the first
Birds of Prey trailer sees Harley Quinn lying

00:01:21.190 --> 00:01:25.810
in what appears to be her own apartment throwing
knives at a crude picture of her ex that she's

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:27.060
pinned to the wall.

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:31.920
The drawing resembles Jared Leto's Joker,
though Harley neglected to draw on his tacky

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:33.160
forehead tattoo.

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:35.420
Yeah, you remember that thing.

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:40.300
Suicide Squad director David Ayer attempted
to make his version of the Joker stand out

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:44.800
from the rest by giving him plenty of ink
and a shiny mouth grill for good measure.

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:49.110
But he later admitted that having the word
"damaged" tattooed across the Joker's forehead

00:01:49.110 --> 00:01:50.910
was kind of one step too far.

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:52.110
He wrote on Twitter,

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:57.050
"In my mind it was meant for Batman after
he smashed Joker's teeth for killing Jason

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:59.720
Todd, [but] some people found it alienating."

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:05.080
For us, this toning down of the Joker's worst
excesses seems like another instance of Birds

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:09.840
of Prey distancing itself from Suicide Squad,
even though we likely wouldn't be getting

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:14.519
this movie at all if that one hadn't first
laid the groundwork for Harley's most fantabulous

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:15.640
emancipation.

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:21.100
Dinah Lance, a.k.a Black Canary is one of
the original members of the Birds of Prey

00:02:21.109 --> 00:02:26.439
in DC's "New 52" continuity, and the Birds
of Prey movie seems to be taking inspiration

00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:31.520
from this version of the character, who's
being portrayed on screen by Jurnee Smollett-Bell.

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:35.540
Lance appears early in the trailer, chatting
with Harley over a drink.

00:02:35.540 --> 00:02:40.560
It seems like this may be a scene of Dinah
being recruited onto Harley's new team.

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:45.520
We see several snippets of Lance performing
onstage during the trailer, which won't come

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:47.380
as a surprise to DC fans.

00:02:47.380 --> 00:02:52.460
In the comics, the character fronts a band
named Black Canary, and DC has even overseen

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:56.220
the production and release of real music by
the fictional group.

00:02:56.220 --> 00:03:00.520
This being a comic book universe, she also
doubles as a crimefighter.

00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:06.240
Her signature metahuman superpower is her
sonic scream, known as the Canary Cry, which

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:09.720
is an incapacitating sound that leaves her
enemies helpless.

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:13.920
Eagle-eyed fans will have noticed that the
movie version will have this power, too.

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:18.780
In the trailer, we see a martini glass start
to shake as the vigilante sings on stage,

00:03:18.780 --> 00:03:21.500
but we cut away before she hits the high note.

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:26.520
Ewan McGregor is playing the big bad in Birds
of Prey.

00:03:26.530 --> 00:03:32.040
His character, Roman Sionis, goes by Black
Mask in the comics because he wears, you guessed

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:33.520
it, a black mask.

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:35.720
"Yeah, that's…that's what that means."

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:40.380
McGregor's version of the character won't
be totally comic book accurate when it comes

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:41.380
to appearance.

00:03:41.380 --> 00:03:46.600
On the page, his mask is burned into his skin
so severely that it's actually indistinguishable

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:47.920
from his actual face.

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:53.220
Adding some extra "grim dark-ness" is the
fact that the mask's material was carved from

00:03:53.220 --> 00:03:54.640
his mother's coffin.

00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:58.860
Considering we see plenty of McGregor's face
in the trailer, that clearly isn't the case

00:03:58.860 --> 00:04:03.500
here, but there is some subtle foreshadowing
about the look Sionis may adopt.

00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:09.100
In the comics, this Gotham mob boss is known
for being mentally unstable, and it appears

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:12.100
as though McGregor's Black Mask will share
that trait.

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:15.100
At one point, we see him in a state of clear
distress.

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:18.860
Just over his shoulder, a figure with a black
face looms large.

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:23.620
Could this be the moment that Sionis goes
full villain and becomes the Black Mask that

00:04:23.620 --> 00:04:26.140
Harley Quinn and her crew will have to take
out?

00:04:26.140 --> 00:04:31.099
One thing we know for sure is that he has
a fascination with Harley, and one way or

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:34.040
another, he's in the way of her full "emancipation."

00:04:34.280 --> 00:04:35.060
"Miss Quinn?

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:36.220
She belongs to me."

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:41.300
Sticking with the villains, there's a shot
of Sionis talking to Victor Zsasz, a psychotic

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:43.220
serial killer from the comics.

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:47.520
This won't be his first movie appearance,
he was a supporting villain in Christopher

00:04:47.530 --> 00:04:53.560
Nolan's Batman Begins, escaping from Arkham
Asylum during Scarecrow and Ra's al Ghul's

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:55.680
short-lived reign of terror.

00:04:55.680 --> 00:05:01.240
He's also been seen in the Gotham TV series
as a right-hand man in Carmine Falcone's crime

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:04.940
syndicate, and it appears as though he'll
be doing the same thing in Birds of Prey.

00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:09.440
The version of Mr. Zsasz being portrayed by
Chris Messina looks different from those that

00:05:09.449 --> 00:05:14.270
came before him, but DC fans can likely figure
out who he is from his scars.

00:05:14.270 --> 00:05:19.450
Zsasz was born to a wealthy family, but after
he lost his parents in an accident he fell

00:05:19.450 --> 00:05:22.080
into a deep depression and squandered his
fortune.

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:27.000
He went down a dark path and became a serial
killer, making a cut on his arm to mark his

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:29.560
first victim…and he didn't stop there.

00:05:29.560 --> 00:05:34.479
The comic book character has hundreds of scars
on his body, keeping a tally of all the people

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:35.480
he's killed.

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:39.940
Does Harley Quinn have a pair of pet hyenas?

00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:44.020
Of course she has a pair of pet hyenas, and
we get a good look at one of them in the first

00:05:44.020 --> 00:05:44.700
trailer.

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:50.800
Like Harley Quinn herself, Bud and Lou, named
after legendary comedy duo Abbott and Costello,

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:56.060
make their debut in Batman: The Animated Series,
but would later cross over to DC's comics.

00:05:56.060 --> 00:06:01.580
At one stage both were stolen by thieves who
attempted to auction them off, but Quinn located

00:06:01.580 --> 00:06:03.960
her babies and put an end to the racket.

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:07.300
It looks as though a version of this will
play out in the movie.

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:12.199
Quinn previously has been shown acquiring
Bud and Lou during a raid of the Gotham Zoo,

00:06:12.199 --> 00:06:17.259
but in the Birds of Prey trailer, she appears
to get at least one of her hyenas from some

00:06:17.260 --> 00:06:19.160
kind of exotic animal dealer.

00:06:19.160 --> 00:06:24.540
In a later shot, the animal runs at the dealer
who, we can only assume, meets a violent end.

00:06:24.540 --> 00:06:29.140
In one of the trailer's standout shots, Quinn
shares what looks like a piece of candy with

00:06:29.140 --> 00:06:31.260
her new pet, Lady and the Tramp style.

00:06:31.480 --> 00:06:34.280
There's a musical feel to the Birds of Prey
trailer.

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:38.639
Not only do we see Jurnee Smollett-Bell's
Black Canary performing at a club that seems

00:06:38.640 --> 00:06:40.100
to be important to the plot.

00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:45.039
It seems pretty clear that it's owned by Ewan
McGregor's Black Mask, who asks patrons if

00:06:45.039 --> 00:06:48.970
they're having a good time, but Harley Quinn
herself has a song and dance number in which

00:06:48.970 --> 00:06:53.720
she channels Marilyn Monroe's performance
of "Diamonds Are a Girl's Best Friend" from

00:06:53.720 --> 00:06:59.220
the 1953 film Gentlemen Prefer Blondes, though
it's a much darker version.

00:06:59.220 --> 00:07:03.780
Quinn has a typically deranged look on her
face during the routine, and the suited men

00:07:03.780 --> 00:07:06.100
surrounding her all wear black masks.

00:07:06.100 --> 00:07:10.580
We know that Sionis has a thing for Quinn,
could he convince her to start working for

00:07:10.580 --> 00:07:11.800
him at the club?

00:07:11.800 --> 00:07:17.160
Harley goes through a number of costume changes
in the trailer, none of which are as ridiculously

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:22.200
revealing as her Suicide Squad outfit, but
we can't see her agreeing to wear this particular

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:23.020
getup.

00:07:23.020 --> 00:07:28.100
This scene is most likely some kind of dream
or nightmare sequence, inspired by her fear

00:07:28.100 --> 00:07:29.500
of the film's antagonist.

00:07:29.500 --> 00:07:33.080
If that's true, however, it obviously won't
last.

00:07:33.080 --> 00:07:34.759
As Harley puts it in the trailer,

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:37.260
"I'm the one they should be scared of!"

00:07:37.800 --> 00:07:42.420
She isn't known for being a member of the
Birds of Prey in the comics, but Renée Montoya,

00:07:42.440 --> 00:07:46.240
played by Rosie Perez, looks like she'll fit
right in to the movie squad.

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:50.340
On the page, the character starts out as a
no-nonsense cop, but she ends up quitting

00:07:50.340 --> 00:07:53.760
the Gotham City Police Department when she
grows tired of the corruption.

00:07:53.760 --> 00:07:57.760
Judging from one of the shots we see of her
in the trailer, she's going to leave the force

00:07:57.770 --> 00:08:02.320
pretty early in the movie; she can be seen
walking though a room full of male cops with

00:08:02.320 --> 00:08:05.860
a box under her arm, seemingly having cleared
out her desk.

00:08:05.860 --> 00:08:10.720
In the comics, Montoya eventually takes on
the moniker the Question, originally used

00:08:10.720 --> 00:08:15.180
by an investigative journalist who sought
to end corruption by any means necessary.

00:08:15.180 --> 00:08:19.539
She's also known for being openly gay, though
there's nothing in the first full Birds of

00:08:19.540 --> 00:08:23.000
Prey trailer to suggest that aspect of her
character just yet.

00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:29.539
Her superhero costume isn't quite as purple
as it is in the comics, but a few small things

00:08:29.539 --> 00:08:35.180
in the Birds of Prey trailer suggest Mary
Elizabeth Winstead's Helena Bertinelli, a.k.a

00:08:35.180 --> 00:08:38.540
Huntress, will be somewhat faithful to the
source material.

00:08:38.540 --> 00:08:42.779
Some of the details are more obvious than
others; she's going to ride a motorcycle and

00:08:42.780 --> 00:08:44.780
wield a crossbow, for example.

00:08:44.780 --> 00:08:49.620
In the comics, Helena, a so-called "mafia
princess" of the Bertinelli crime family,

00:08:49.620 --> 00:08:54.450
was taken in by her Sicilian aunt and uncle
after her family was massacred, and they taught

00:08:54.450 --> 00:08:59.180
her archery among other skills that she'd
later put to use as a vigilante in Gotham.

00:08:59.180 --> 00:09:03.640
Another Huntress character trait is that she's
a deeply religious person.

00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:08.580
This leads us to believe that the third shot
in the trailer, of a woman praying in a church,

00:09:08.580 --> 00:09:09.620
is Bertinelli.

00:09:09.620 --> 00:09:13.980
We only see her from behind, but at this early
stage in the trailer the ladies that will

00:09:13.990 --> 00:09:18.339
become the Birds of Prey are clearly being
introduced, and DC fans have been able to

00:09:18.340 --> 00:09:19.520
figure this one out.

00:09:19.520 --> 00:09:24.440
In a later shot, a woman wearing what appears
to be the same modest outfit is strung upside

00:09:24.440 --> 00:09:29.950
down alongside two other females by Black
Mask, so she appears to have previous contact

00:09:29.950 --> 00:09:32.820
with the villain prior to hooking up with
Harley Quinn and the gang.

00:09:33.020 --> 00:09:37.440
In the comics, Cassandra Cain is a member
of the Bat-family, at one point taking on

00:09:37.440 --> 00:09:38.960
the mantle of Batgirl.

00:09:38.960 --> 00:09:43.580
But the version of Cassandra we see in the
Birds of Prey trailer seems pretty far removed

00:09:43.580 --> 00:09:45.760
from the badass she is on the page.

00:09:45.760 --> 00:09:51.180
In DC's comics, Cain is a talented martial
artist, raised by assassin parents who taught

00:09:51.180 --> 00:09:53.840
her how to fight instead of teaching her how
to speak.

00:09:53.840 --> 00:09:58.700
But Ella Jay Basco's version of the character
can clearly talk in the film's first trailer,

00:09:58.700 --> 00:10:01.720
so we know that she won't be mute in the movie.

00:10:01.720 --> 00:10:07.140
The big-screen Cassandra Cain must have something
about her, however, because Black Mask appears

00:10:07.150 --> 00:10:09.360
to be after her for some reason.

00:10:09.360 --> 00:10:14.490
The plot of Birds of Prey seems like it revolves
around the team protecting Cain from the ruthless

00:10:14.490 --> 00:10:19.250
crime lord by any means necessary, with the
youngster becoming a reluctant sidekick to

00:10:19.250 --> 00:10:20.720
Harley Quinn along the way.

00:10:21.080 --> 00:10:22.080
"Oh, you're that psycho chick."

00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:24.120
"You never call a woman a chick."

00:10:24.300 --> 00:10:26.860
